---
import { Code } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
import example from './bash-syntax.json';
---
<p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> configure the Bash preset and put Bash on <code>PATH</code>.</p>
<div class="comparison">
    <section aria-labelledby="defect">
        <h3 id="defect">Defect</h3>
        <p>The <code>if</code> statement has no condition. The check reports <code>bash/syntax</code>.</p>
        <Code frame="code" code={example.broken.trimEnd()} lang="bash" title="greet.sh" />
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="correction">
        <h3 id="correction">Manual correction</h3>
        <p>Replace the file contents with a valid command.</p>
        <Code frame="code" code={example.corrected.trimEnd()} lang="bash" title="greet.sh" />
    </section>
</div>
<p>From the configured repository root, run this command before and after the correction:</p>
<Code frame="code" code="gspot check --only bash/syntax --no-cache" lang="sh" />
<p>The corrected file produces no findings. Follow the <a href="/guides/quick-start/">first-check guide</a>{' '}for the complete setup.</p>
<details>
    <summary>Captured command output</summary>
    <p>Captured with gspot {example.version}, {example.platform}, Bash on PATH, and caching {example.cache}.
        Only Bash syntax was checked.</p>
    <p>Output before the manual correction:</p>
    <Code frame="code" code={example.failed.trimEnd()} lang="text" />
    <p>Output after the manual correction and the same check command:</p>
    <Code frame="code" code={example.passed.trimEnd()} lang="text" />
</details>

<style>
    .comparison {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
        gap: 24px;
        margin-block: 24px;
        border-radius: 8px;
        box-shadow: 0 0 64px -24px rgb(59 130 246 / 25%);
    }
    .comparison > section { min-width: 0; margin: 0; }
    h3 { font-size: 1.125rem; }
    details { margin-top: 24px; }
    @media (max-width: 40rem) {
        .comparison { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    }
</style>
